shapeprojector:gui-tip-addout:
Copies layer {0} and grows the copy one block outward, then selects the copy.
{1}
The Y offset does not move (Y {2}). Each press adds the next ring out, filling toward a solid disc.

shapeprojector:gui-tip-globalplus:
One step OUTWARD applied to every layer at once — disabled ones included, so hidden work never drifts out of step. Y offsets are never touched.
Layer {0}: {1}
All layers: {2}

shapeprojector:gui-tip-globalminus:
One step INWARD applied to every layer at once — disabled ones included, so hidden work never drifts out of step. Y offsets are never touched.
Layer {0}: {1}
All layers: {2}
A layer already at its smallest stays exactly as it is, so −1 then +1 is not a round trip: that layer ends one step larger than it began.
